--- A row whose items nothing typed is any row, read as its push takes it,
--- and so is one whose items can fail and nothing typed: `place` is called
--- by no one, so `x` is not known, and `wide[t] + x` is a number that can
--- fail of no kind yet. It had been refused as "a list whose items can
--- fail" pushed to a matrix, in both modes, and in a test of a program
--- that leaves the function out (Lory's pass, the canvas nothing made).
fn wide[t]
    if t eq 'odd'
        return error['odd']
    1.5

fn place[x, t]
    rows = slice[[[0.0, 0.0]], 0, 0]
    tw = wide[t] + x
    rows = push[rows, [tw, x]]
    len[rows]

log[wide['even']]
